        "id": 4159917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T18:52:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the original four-size restriction came from zune-jpeg. I have extended upstream PR498 to cover every reduced n/8 ratio using native-compatible integer IDCTs, including enlarged chroma transforms, rather than resizing full-size pixels. Chromium prerequisite CL8708834 backports that extension. Skia now advertises all eight sizes and matches every native selection threshold. All 96 additional whole-image RGB comparisons were byte-exact. The corresponding Blink CL8652942 is being updated to enumerate all eighth steps too, so a 128x128 image requested at 96x96 can select 96x96 rather than 64x64. Finite-memory-budget and auxiliary-image requests retain their existing native fallback. Both Skia wrappers continue to cap advertised dimensions at full size; native library upscaling is not exposed here.",
      "parentUuid": "809c0688_1480354f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 325,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 327,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "isAi": true,
