      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T17:17:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No scaled scanline decoding - is this a zune limitation?\n\n`SkCodec::startScanlineDecode` calls `dimensionsSupported()` which would accept one of the fractional sizes, but then `onStartScanlineDecode()` rejects them and the scanline decode fails.  The same holds if the client tries to query a suitable size, and AFAICT there is no way to query a guaranteed size for scanline decoding.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 966,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 968,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "4193aacbe3fde23e33ac3a79d8ece0741f58e997",
