      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T17:17:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are the side effects here for default-initialized decoders (`input_complete` \u003d\u003d false)?\n\nIt seems they are being switched to incremental mode, where EOF is recoverable and truncated (or partially downloaded) packed jpeg decoding can fail with kIncompleteInput instead of producing best-effort output?\n\nIs there a way to preserve the legacy best-effort behavior?",
      "revId": "4193aacbe3fde23e33ac3a79d8ece0741f58e997",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4dfa9567_ff627ad9",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_jpeg/ffi/FFI.rs",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 866,
      "author": {
        "id": 4159917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-03T18:52:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right: enabling incremental mode unconditionally changed legacy one-shot EOF recovery. I removed that blanket switch and restored the full-frame non-incremental, non-strict best-effort policy, including for default-initialized stream decoders and generic SkCodec::MakeFromData dispatch. Scaled decoding now chooses incremental policy by operation, not just the input flag. New regressions use the incomplete progressive DC fixture: one-shot decoding reconstructs the native gray frame, while growing incremental decoding remains incomplete and leaves the unstable destination untouched until a real EOI arrives. A best-effort getPixels call does not promote later incremental sessions to complete input.",
      "parentUuid": "f1955f90_1f29715a",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4193aacbe3fde23e33ac3a79d8ece0741f58e997",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
